  "revolver38": {
   "_doc": "The .38 Special's actions, ported 2026-11-10 from the approved AE showcase design (AE_Weapon_Renders/audio/build_38.py ACTIONS; audition hammer_old_then_new.wav). Exact slices (cut = [start, end] s of the source, contact = the transient the anchor sits on, pitch in st, hp in Hz; build_elements.cut_variant): no onset snap, no transient designer. Keys follow Revolver38.controller (snd.revolver38.*): cock -> hammer_cock, decock -> hammer_decock, cyl_open -> crane_open, cyl_close -> crane_close, eject -> ejector, insert -> round_insert, spin -> cylinder_spin. Hammer cock: the R08's own ratchet then the sear catch (2.7745 s) from its empty reload, +1.5 / +2.2 st, thin (hp 900), quiet. Decock: single real dry-fire clicks (Steyr TMP, Pole Position Production), same treatment, a touch quieter. Levels: mix.json levels.elements. Added 2026-11-10 (not in the showcase): cloth / handle = the soft movement and hand-on-frame grabs of the Kinemation pack's MKR9 pistol handling (draw / holster / inspect; SFX/Kinemation, sfx/ in adsp) and its General pistol draw - the R08's own handling takes sit only 24-35 dB over their hiss (the AK's 40-57 dB; these and the 870's: digital silence between events), so normalized they hissed; dry_fire = a double-action pull on an empty chamber: the R08's cylinder-hand ratchet (just before the sear catch of hammer_cock, +1.5 / +2 st, thin) and a real hammer-fall click (the Steyr TMP dry-fire takes the AK uses) ~85 ms later; melee_swing = the AK's lighter swings, pitched up for a small gun; melee_hit = the AK's punch / thud layers with R08 metal (the cylinder slamming shut, the crane seating) in place of the AK's. These use the shared levels (mix.json levels.elements cloth / handle / dry_fire, levels.melee_*).",
